  "problem": "A company is selling a new product on three e-commerce platforms, platform $1,$ platform $2,$ and platform $3.$\n\n- $44%$ of customers bought the product on platform $1,$ and $70%$ of those customers were satisfied with the product.\n\n- $25%$ of customers bought the product on platform $2,$ and $85%$ of those customers were satisfied with the product.\n\n- $31%$ of customers bought the product on platform $3.$\n\nIf $25%$ of all customers are teenagers, $60%$ of teenage customers are satisfied with the product, and $20%$ of satisfied customers are teenagers, what is the probability that a randomly chosen customer from platform $3$ is satisfied? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
